00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:02.690
So I'll just explain a
little bit about Anthos

00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:05.440
as an abstraction of Kubernetes.

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:08.090
So Anthos is a
Kubernetes platform

00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:10.310
that can run on Google Cloud.

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:12.560
It can run on-prem
and it can also

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:14.540
run on other Cloud
providers and still

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:16.940
have a single pane of
glass for a platform team

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:18.829
to manage that infrastructure.

00:04:18.829 --> 00:04:20.540
And then Cloud Run
for Anthos runs

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:24.200
on top of Anthos,
further abstracting

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:26.190
Kubernetes from the developers.

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:28.940
So it creates a
separation of concerns--

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:30.890
platform teams
care about Anthos,

00:04:30.890 --> 00:04:33.560
that's the platform they
run, and then the developers

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:36.500
care about Cloud Run for
Anthos because that's

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:39.210
their lens that
they see the Cloud

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:41.880
and on-prem
infrastructure through.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.390
Jeenal, could you
