00:04:44.390 --> 00:04:46.673
about how it works
for a developer?

00:04:46.673 --> 00:04:49.340
A little bit about what their "a
day in the life of a developer"

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:50.750
would be?

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:52.940
JEENAL SHAH: Absolutely,
and I'm happy to share

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:58.310
what all features Cloud Run for
Anthos comes out of the box.

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:01.810
Cloud Run for Anthos is tightly
integrated with Cloud Builder

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:06.110
and under the covers uses
industry-standard Cloud-native

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:10.220
specification that allows you
to build applications directly

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:13.130
from source code and deploy.

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:15.740
You can also directly
deploy your Docker

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:17.660
containerised applications.

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:22.370
You don't need to learn
kubectl or Knative commands.

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:28.850
It is directly integrated with
G-Cloud CLI or Google Cloud

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:30.980
Platform UI.

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:35.030
The other features that I
am really passionate about

00:05:35.030 --> 00:05:39.260
is talking about gradual
rollouts, rollbacks,

00:05:39.260 --> 00:05:41.360
and traffic
migrations, and why I'm

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:44.300
so excited because it
brings out of the box

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:47.225
Google's SRE's best practices.

00:05:47.225 --> 00:05:49.430
Cloud Run for Anthos
allow you to roll out

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:52.400
new revisions of your
applications or services

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:54.770
you perform with
simple A/B testing,

00:05:54.770 --> 00:05:58.610
canary testing by specify
which revision should receive

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:00.440
what percentage of traffic.

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:03.110
It allows you to roll back
to our previous versions

00:06:03.110 --> 00:06:05.090
gradually throughout
your revision,

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:08.240
or split traffic between
multiple revisions.

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:11.750
And with this, you can
directly either use

00:06:11.750 --> 00:06:17.210
our continuous deployment or
integrate that with your CI/CD.

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:21.290
It also comes tightly integrated
with Cloud Monitoring and Cloud

00:06:21.290 --> 00:06:23.240
Logging out of the box.

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:25.640
It provides a metrics
collection dashboard

00:06:25.640 --> 00:06:29.060
so that you can gain visibility
into your performance

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:33.140
availability, health of your
services, and infrastructures.

00:06:33.140 --> 00:06:37.310
Because it uses an
OpenTelemetry agent,

00:06:37.310 --> 00:06:40.070
it is possible to
also send metrics

00:06:40.070 --> 00:06:43.700
to any compatible third
party monitoring solutions.

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:46.940
So we have some
amazing features that

00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:49.490
comes right out of the box.

00:06:49.490 --> 00:06:54.080
And, yeah, we will see
some of this during a demo.

