Since we have an existing
service already deployed,

00:13:16.850 --> 00:13:18.770
we're going to tell
Cloud Run for Anthos

00:13:18.770 --> 00:13:20.850
that we'd like to
add something to it.

00:13:20.850 --> 00:13:24.110
So in this case, we already had
the blue app container image.

00:13:24.110 --> 00:13:29.450
I'm going to replace that with
the green app container image.

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:35.980
And is there anything else
I need to change, Jeenal?

00:13:35.980 --> 00:13:38.260
JEENAL SHAH: Yeah, so
let's make sure to disable

00:13:38.260 --> 00:13:41.110
automatic rollout so
we can use traffic

00:13:41.110 --> 00:13:43.750
splitting for granular
control of the traffic

00:13:43.750 --> 00:13:45.800
to a new revision.

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:47.280
MICAH BAKER: OK.

00:13:47.280 --> 00:13:48.630
JEENAL SHAH: That's the one.

00:13:48.630 --> 00:13:49.630
MICAH BAKER: Right here.

00:13:49.630 --> 00:13:53.630
So, yeah, we want to start
off with 0% traffic to this

00:13:53.630 --> 00:13:57.680
since our intent is an A/B test.

00:13:57.680 --> 00:14:00.110
That will say,
create this revision,

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:02.720
but we're not going to
serve anything, right?

00:14:02.720 --> 00:14:04.070
JEENAL SHAH: Correct.

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:05.612
MICAH BAKER: All
right, let's deploy.

00:14:08.400 --> 00:14:10.680
And now it's grabbing
that container image.

00:14:14.170 --> 00:14:16.810
OK, so that looked easy.

00:14:16.810 --> 00:14:19.750
We can use this
Manage Traffic button

00:14:19.750 --> 00:14:21.280
to control the traffic split.

00:14:21.280 --> 00:14:23.350
And notice that
we're already serving

00:14:23.350 --> 00:14:28.680
100% from the initial revision,
which was our blue app.

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:31.270
Jeenal, what do you
recommend for this demo

00:14:31.270 --> 00:14:33.640
versus what we would do in
production for this traffic

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:34.510
split?

00:14:34.510 --> 00:14:36.490
JEENAL SHAH: Yeah,
so to make it easier

00:14:36.490 --> 00:14:40.810
to see the traffic splitting
at work, let's go with 50%

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:42.730
to each revision.

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:44.650
What do you think?

00:14:44.650 --> 00:14:46.450
MICAH BAKER: That sounds good.

00:14:46.450 --> 00:14:47.600
Oh, yeah, look at that.

00:14:47.600 --> 00:14:51.100
I changed the new one to 50%
and automatically balanced

00:14:51.100 --> 00:14:54.550
out the percentages.

00:14:54.550 --> 00:14:59.282
50-50 is great because for demo
purposes of the blue green app

00:14:59.282 --> 00:15:01.240
that we're doing, that
will make it really easy

00:15:01.240 --> 00:15:04.720
to see the traffic split.

00:15:04.720 --> 00:15:06.130
JEENAL SHAH: Yeah.

00:15:06.130 --> 00:15:08.660
Yeah, and for the
production, of course,

00:15:08.660 --> 00:15:10.990
we wouldn't recommend
that, and would instead

00:15:10.990 --> 00:15:13.270
follow the Google
SRE best practices

00:15:13.270 --> 00:15:16.780
for the class of application
and potentially plan a five day

00:15:16.780 --> 00:15:19.210
gradual rollout
that begins with 1%,

00:15:19.210 --> 00:15:24.220
and then graduates daily
to a larger percentage.

00:15:24.220 --> 00:15:26.170
MICAH BAKER: I
appreciate the call

00:15:26.170 --> 00:15:28.240
out to Google SRE
best practices, which

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:30.550
we are certainly not
following in this demo

00:15:30.550 --> 00:15:34.400
if we jump straight to 50% if
this was production traffic.

00:15:34.400 --> 00:15:39.792
But this will be a great
way for us to just showcase

00:15:39.792 --> 00:15:40.750
this traffic splitting.

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:42.220
So let's see what happened.

00:15:42.220 --> 00:15:44.320
I'm going to open up the app.

00:15:44.320 --> 00:15:47.080
And look, we already
got the green app.

00:15:47.080 --> 00:15:48.610
I'm going to refresh.

00:15:48.610 --> 00:15:49.900
And look at that.

00:15:49.900 --> 00:15:52.240
The first refresh switched
me to the blue app.

00:15:52.240 --> 00:15:55.000
So both of them are
running, and it's just

00:15:55.000 --> 00:15:58.180
alternating between
the two as it randomly

00:15:58.180 --> 00:16:01.910
does a 50% split for
any incoming requests.

00:16:01.910 --> 00:16:03.550
So that's a pretty
quick and easy way

00:16:03.550 --> 00:16:07.330
to do any kind of A/B tests.

00:16:07.330 --> 00:16:11.020
Let's go back here then.

00:16:11.020 --> 00:16:14.470
Jeenal, what do you think we
should do next since we-- it

00:16:14.470 --> 00:16:18.190
looks to me from an end user
perspective like the 50% split

00:16:18.190 --> 00:16:18.723
is working.

00:16:18.723 --> 00:16:20.890
Is there anything else that
you would want to check?

00:16:20.890 --> 00:16:23.080
JEENAL SHAH: Yeah, so
let's look at the metrics

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:27.760
and log to confirm that what
we see here, we like it,

00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:32.114
and then progress the rollout.

00:16:32.114 --> 00:16:33.050
Yeah.

00:16:33.050 --> 00:16:37.310
MICAH BAKER: So I just jumped
right to a one hour view

00:16:37.310 --> 00:16:39.800
since that makes
sense to me of what

00:16:39.800 --> 00:16:42.630
we've just been working on.

00:16:42.630 --> 00:16:43.870
Yeah.

00:16:43.870 --> 00:16:48.160
JEENAL SHAH: Yeah, and
can we also quickly--

00:16:48.160 --> 00:16:50.470
or, Micah, can you
